cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "airmkit: Operationalising the MAS Guidelines on AI Risk Management for LLM and Agentic Systems"
message: "If you use this toolkit or its catalogue, crosswalk or results, please cite it."
type: software
license: Apache-2.0
version: 0.1.0
date-released: "2026-10-13"
repository-code: "https://github.com/thanatchon36/airmkit"
url: "https://thanatchon36.github.io/airmkit/"
authors:
  - family-names: Chongmankhong
    given-names: Thanatchon
abstract: >-
  An open-source Python toolkit and reproducible study that operationalise the Monetary Authority
  of Singapore's Guidelines on Artificial Intelligence Risk Management (7 October 2026) for LLM
  and agentic AI systems. It ships a machine-readable catalogue of all 65 paragraphs, 65 controls
  each citing the paragraph it serves, an AI inventory schema with first-class agent attributes, a
  transparent Impact/Complexity/Reliance materiality rubric, hash-chained evidence records,
  adapters from existing evaluation harnesses to controls, a 224-row crosswalk to ISO/IEC 42001,
  the NIST AI RMF and its Generative AI Profile, the EU AI Act, MAS FEAT and the MAS Information
  Paper (2024), and an audit-pack generator. Five pre-registered experiments measure how far the
  Guidelines can be machine-checked; seven of seventeen hypotheses were refuted and all are
  reported. Independent project, not affiliated with or endorsed by MAS, and not legal advice.
keywords:
  - ai-governance
  - model-risk
  - mas
  - llm-evaluation
  - agentic-ai
  - compliance
  - guardrails
